---
name: discover
description: Structural codebase navigation via ast-grep. Routes to language-specific subskills. Use `discover/<lang>` for language-specific commands.
argument-hint: <lang> | langs
---

## Installed languages

Check which language scripts are installed:

```bash
{{WRAPPER_PATH}} langs
```

## Dispatch

Use the language subskill directly:

- `discover/<lang>` — e.g. `discover/swift`, `discover/typescript`, `discover/ruby`

Or use the wrapper script (auto-detects language from file extension):

```bash
{{WRAPPER_PATH}} inspect <file>
{{WRAPPER_PATH}} usages '<pattern>'
{{WRAPPER_PATH}} definition <file> <symbol>
```

## Available subcommands (all languages)

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `resolve <import>` | Resolve an import to a repo-relative path |
| `inspect <file>` | Extract structured JSON (imports, entities) |
| `definition <file> <symbol>` | Find where a symbol is defined |
| `live-files` | List files reachable from entry point |
| `is-live <file>` | Check if a file is reachable |
| `importers <file>` | Find all files that import a file |
| `usages <pattern>` | Structural search for an ast-grep pattern |

See the language-specific subskill for examples, caveats, and full usage.
